  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"IRQ handler. With raster_split_enable set and a raster interrupt, it makes the menu screen splits: from line 0 white background and multicolour, from line $b2 hires, from line $ca mix_colour as background. Else (the CIA 1 timer): UDTIM, the pad read, the button state, the menu flash, the idle tick sound, the cursor colour and SCNKEY, each when its flag is set."},
    {"at":1,"placement":"side","text":"raster_split_enable"},
    {"at":5,"placement":"side","text":"the raster interrupt flag"},
    {"at":15,"placement":"side","text":"line $ca or below: bottom part"},
    {"at":19,"placement":"side","text":"background of the bottom part = mix_colour"},
    {"at":26,"placement":"side","text":"next interrupt at line 0"},
    {"at":32,"placement":"side","text":"line $b2 or below: middle part"},
    {"at":39,"placement":"side","text":"multicolour off"},
    {"at":46,"placement":"side","text":"next interrupt at line $ca"},
    {"at":54,"placement":"side","text":"top part: white background"},
    {"at":60,"placement":"side","text":"multicolour on"},
    {"at":67,"placement":"side","text":"next interrupt at line $b2"},
    {"at":79,"placement":"side","text":"acknowledge the CIA 1 interrupt"},
    {"at":82,"placement":"side","text":"bits 2 and 3: the pad buttons (port 1 left and right lines, low = down)"},
    {"at":96,"placement":"side","text":"set button_press_edge only on the first interrupt with the button down"},
    {"at":120,"placement":"side","text":"pad_untouched"},
    {"at":136,"placement":"side","text":"a tick sound each 33 interrupts"},
    {"at":172,"placement":"side","text":"acknowledge the raster interrupt"},
    {"at":175,"placement":"side","text":"restore Y, X and A that the KERNAL IRQ entry pushed"},
    {"at":181,"placement":"line","text":"IRQ part: when pad_read_enable is not 0, reads POT X and POT Y into pad_x_raw and pad_y_raw and moves the 5 samples of each axis one place down."},
    {"at":212,"placement":"line","text":"IRQ part: counts flash_timer down. At 0 it calls FLASHEM and sets flash_timer to 20 again."},
    {"at":226,"placement":"line","text":"IRQ part: counts cursor_colour_timer down. At 0 it calls $19da (the cursor sprite colours from the sprite-background collision) and sets the timer to 2 again."}
  ],
